/**
\mainpage FCG Framework

The FCG Framework is a lightweight C++ graphics framework used as the basis for all practical assignments of the
<em>Foundations Computer Graphics</em> exercise. It is built around the <em>SDL 3 GPU</em> API, a modern rendering
middleware with backends for Vulkan, Direct3D 12 and Metal.

The functionality is grouped by purpose into the <em>Core</em>, <em>Image</em>, <em>Render</em>, and <em>Extras</em>
libraries. Each library has an overview page describing its purpose and where to start. The module guides then give
step-by-step usage guidance for every part of a library.

\section fcg_start Start here

Begin with the \ref fcg_core_overview "Core overview": it shows how to write a first applet and run it with
\ref fcg::run, and points to the modules for input handling, geometry, images, cameras, and GUI.

\section fcg_library_overviews Library overviews

- \ref fcg_core_overview "Core library overview"
- \ref fcg_image_overview "Image library overview"
- \ref fcg_render_overview "Render library overview"
- \ref fcg_extras_overview "Extras library overview"

\section fcg_modules_section Module guides

All module guides are collected under \ref fcg_modules. The library pages under \ref fcg_libraries list which modules
belong to which library, together with the CMake link target to use.

\section fcg_api API reference

Browse the <a href="annotated.html">class reference</a>, <a href="namespaces.html">namespaces</a>, and
<a href="files.html">public headers</a>.
*/

/** \defgroup fcg_modules Modules
 * The framework's module guides. Each guide is a group with its own page and holds the usage guidance for one module;
 * there is roughly one module per public header. The library pages under \ref fcg_libraries show which library
 * provides which module.
 */
